@*
    Risk Methodology -- migration 532 (2026-11-12).

    Screen key : `risk-methodology`
    Group      : Risk Management (533)
    Menu       : risk-centre (Risk Management) -> risk-centre-settings
                 (Settings) -> Risk Methodology; under nav-organization
                 before 533

    The organisation's own risk methodology: the extra dimensions the
    scoring pages ask (velocity, proximity, persistence, control
    effectiveness, confidence, or its own), the scoring mode (matrix,
    priority, 3D), appetite, target rating, impact by area, trend and
    quantification.

    VERSIONED. The published version is what the risk pages use. Changes
    are made to a Draft (started from the published version or from a
    template) and Publish makes the draft the next version. Assessments
    keep the version they were made under.

    Follows risk-settings' conventions: pm-page-heading compact, an org
    picker in a pm-toolbar, pm-panel sections, pm-table-wrap grids.
    Edit = the organisation administrator (menu EDIT on this screen; the
    Web proxy refuses the writes otherwise).

    Backend:
        GET  /practice/api/risk-centre/methodology?organizationId=
        POST /practice/api/risk-centre/methodology/draft          { organizationId, templateCode, replace }
        POST /practice/api/risk-centre/methodology/draft/save     { organizationId, draft }
        POST /practice/api/risk-centre/methodology/draft/discard  { organizationId }
        POST /practice/api/risk-centre/methodology/publish        { organizationId }
*@
@model PracticeManagement.Web.Models.PracticeScreen

<div class="pm-page-heading compact">
    <div>
        <p class="pm-eyebrow">@Model.Group / @Model.Title</p>
        <h1>@Model.Title</h1>
        <p>
            How this organization assesses risk beyond likelihood and impact. Changes are
            made in a draft and take effect when published; risks keep the version they
            were assessed under.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="pm-panel" id="rmRoot">
    <div class="pm-toolbar pm-toolbar-fields" style="flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px; align-items:end;">
        <label class="pm-field">
            <span>Organization</span>
            <select class="pm-input" id="rmPickOrg" style="min-width:260px;">
                <option value="">Loading...</option>
            </select>
        </label>
        @* Where a new draft starts -- choosing it STARTS the draft, there is
           no separate button (2026-11-12). "Published version" is offered
           only when the organisation has one (risk-methodology.js); "From a
           template" opens the Template combo, and picking a template starts
           the draft. Replacing an open draft asks first. *@
        <label class="pm-field">
            <span>Draft</span>
            <select class="pm-input" id="rmStartFrom" style="min-width:260px;">
                <option value="">-- choose --</option>
                @* Shown and selected while a draft is open: the form below is
                   that draft. Choosing another option replaces it. *@
                <option value="DRAFT">Current draft</option>
                <option value="BLANK">New &mdash; blank</option>
                <option value="PUBLISHED">New &mdash; copy of the published version</option>
                <option value="TEMPLATE">New &mdash; from a template</option>
            </select>
        </label>
        <label class="pm-field" id="rmTemplateWrap" hidden>
            <span>Template</span>
            <select class="pm-input" id="rmTemplate" style="min-width:180px;">
                <option value="">-- choose --</option>
                <option value="ISO31000">ISO 31000</option>
                <option value="COSO_ERM">COSO ERM</option>
                <option value="ISO27005">ISO 27005</option>
            </select>
        </label>
        @* Standard icon refresh button (same markup as the dashboards'
           mdRefreshBtn); .pm-toolbar-fields lines it up with the combos. *@
        <button class="pm-button icon" id="rmReloadBtn" type="button" title="Reload" aria-label="Reload">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </button>
    </div>

    <p class="rm-status" id="rmStatus" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
</section>

<form id="rmForm" hidden>
    @* 2026-11-12: every option is one row, and the configuration an option
       needs (3D bands, impact areas, appetite, currency) opens directly
       beneath it -- not as a separate card further down the page. *@
    <section class="pm-panel">
        <div class="pm-section-heading">
            <h2>Scoring &amp; options</h2>
            <p>How a risk is scored, and what else the risk pages ask.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rm-options">
            <div class="rm-opt">
                <div class="rm-opt-text">
                    <span class="rm-opt-title">Methodology name<span class="pm-required">*</span></span>
                    <span class="rm-opt-hint">Shown on the risk pages and in the version history. Required to publish.</span>
                </div>
                <input class="pm-input rm-opt-control" type="text" id="rmName" maxlength="200" placeholder="e.g. ISMS risk methodology 2026" />
            </div>
            <div class="rm-opt">
                <div class="rm-opt-text">
                    <span class="rm-opt-title">Scoring mode</span>
                    <span class="rm-opt-hint">Matrix keeps likelihood &times; impact. Priority adds a ranking score; the rating does not change. 3D multiplies a third dimension into the score.</span>
                </div>
                <select class="pm-input rm-opt-control" id="rmScoringMode">
                    <option value="Matrix">Matrix (likelihood &times; impact)</option>
                    <option value="Priority">Priority score</option>
                    <option value="3D">3D score</option>
                </select>
            </div>
            <div class="rm-sub" id="rmBandsPanel">
                <div class="rm-sub-row" id="rmThirdWrap">
                    <label class="pm-field">
                        <span>Third dimension</span>
                        <select class="pm-input" id="rmThirdAxis"></select>
                    </label>
                    <p class="rm-sub-hint" id="rmBandsHint">Every score from 1 to the maximum must fall in exactly one band.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pm-table-wrap rm-compact">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th>From score</th><th>To score</th><th>Rating</th><th aria-label="Actions"></th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody id="rmBandBody"></tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <button type="button" class="pm-button ghost rm-add" id="rmAddBand"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i> Add band</button>
            </div>

            <div class="rm-opt">
                <div class="rm-opt-text">
                    <span class="rm-opt-title">Overall impact</span>
                    <span class="rm-opt-hint">One impact for the risk, or impact rated per area with the highest or the average counting.</span>
                </div>
                <select class="pm-input rm-opt-control" id="rmImpactMode">
                    <option value="Single">One impact for the risk</option>
                    <option value="Max">Per area &mdash; highest counts</option>
                    <option value="Average">Per area &mdash; average counts</option>
                </select>
            </div>
            <div class="rm-sub" id="rmAreasPanel">
                <div class="pm-table-wrap rm-compact">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Impact area</th><th aria-label="Actions"></th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody id="rmAreaBody"></tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <button type="button" class="pm-button ghost rm-add" id="rmAddArea"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i> Add impact area</button>
            </div>

            <label class="rm-opt rm-toggle">
                <input type="checkbox" id="rmTarget" />
                <span class="rm-opt-text">
                    <span class="rm-opt-title">Target risk rating</span>
                    <span class="rm-opt-hint">Ask for the rating treatment should reach; the register shows it until the residual rating gets there.</span>
                </span>
            </label>

            <label class="rm-opt rm-toggle">
                <input type="checkbox" id="rmAppetite" />
                <span class="rm-opt-text">
                    <span class="rm-opt-title">Risk appetite</span>
                    <span class="rm-opt-hint">Flag a risk whose current rating (residual, else inherent) is above the highest acceptable rating. A category row overrides the default; with several categories the strictest applies.</span>
                </span>
            </label>
            <div class="rm-sub" id="rmAppetitePanel">
                <div class="pm-table-wrap rm-compact">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Highest acceptable rating</th><th>Appetite statement</th><th aria-label="Actions"></th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody id="rmAppetiteBody"></tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <button type="button" class="pm-button ghost rm-add" id="rmAddAppetite"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i> Add appetite</button>
            </div>

            <label class="rm-opt rm-toggle">
                <input type="checkbox" id="rmTrend" />
                <span class="rm-opt-text">
                    <span class="rm-opt-title">Trend</span>
                    <span class="rm-opt-hint">Show whether the rating went up, down or stayed the same since the previous assessment.</span>
                </span>
            </label>

            <label class="rm-opt rm-toggle">
                <input type="checkbox" id="rmQuant" />
                <span class="rm-opt-text">
                    <span class="rm-opt-title">Quantification</span>
                    <span class="rm-opt-hint">Capture the single loss expectancy and the annual rate; ALE = SLE &times; ARO.</span>
                </span>
            </label>
            <div class="rm-sub" id="rmCurrencyWrap">
                <label class="pm-field rm-currency">
                    <span>Currency</span>
                    <input class="pm-input" type="text" id="rmCurrency" maxlength="10" placeholder="e.g. INR" />
                </label>
            </div>

            <div class="rm-opt rm-opt-notes">
                <div class="rm-opt-text">
                    <span class="rm-opt-title">Notes</span>
                    <span class="rm-opt-hint">Anything the next person editing the methodology should know.</span>
                </div>
                <textarea class="pm-input rm-opt-control" id="rmNotes" rows="2" maxlength="1000"></textarea>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pm-panel">
        <div class="pm-section-heading">
            <h2>Dimensions</h2>
            <p>Asked beside likelihood and impact. For every dimension a <strong>higher level means more risk</strong>. The weight is used by the priority score.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-table-wrap rm-compact">
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>On</th><th>Dimension</th><th>Required</th>
                        <th>Inherent</th><th>Residual</th><th>Review</th>
                        <th>Weight</th><th>Levels</th><th aria-label="Actions"></th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody id="rmDimBody"></tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="pm-button ghost rm-add" id="rmAddDim"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i> Add dimension</button>
    </section>

    <div class="rm-actions">
        <p class="pm-form-message" id="rmMessage" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="rmDiscardBtn">Discard draft</button>
        <button type="submit" class="pm-button" id="rmSaveBtn"><i class="fa-solid fa-floppy-disk"></i> Save draft</button>
        <button type="button" class="pm-button primary" id="rmPublishBtn"><i class="fa-solid fa-upload"></i> Publish</button>
    </div>
</form>

<section class="pm-panel" id="rmHistoryPanel" hidden>
    <div class="pm-section-heading">
        <h2>Version history</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="pm-table-wrap">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Version</th><th>Name</th><th>Status</th><th>Scoring</th><th>Template</th><th>Published</th><th>By</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody id="rmHistoryBody"></tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

<style>
    /* Page-local, like risk-settings' .rs-check (risk-centre.cshtml's
       style block is not loaded on this page). Tokens only. */
    /* .pm-field sets display:grid, which beats the browser's [hidden]. */
    #rmRoot .pm-field[hidden] { display: none; }
    #rmRoot .rm-status { margin: 8px 0 0; font-size: 12px; color: var(--fg-secondary); }

    /* Options: one row each; an option's configuration (.rm-sub) opens
       directly under it. */
    #rmForm .rm-options { display: flex; flex-direction: column; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
    /* One grid for every row: [checkbox | title + hint | control].
       Rows without a checkbox leave the first column empty, so every
       title starts at the same x and every control has the same width
       and right edge. */
    #rmForm .rm-opt {
        display: grid; grid-template-columns: 16px minmax(0, 1fr) 320px;
        column-gap: 12px; align-items: center;
        padding: 10px 4px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); margin: 0;
    }
    #rmForm .rm-opt > .rm-opt-text { grid-column: 2; }
    #rmForm .rm-opt > .rm-opt-control { grid-column: 3; width: 100%; height: 34px; margin: 0; }
    #rmForm .rm-opt > textarea.rm-opt-control { height: auto; min-height: 56px; }
    #rmForm .rm-toggle { cursor: pointer; align-items: start; }
    #rmForm .rm-toggle > input { grid-column: 1; margin: 2px 0 0; width: 16px; height: 16px; }
    #rmForm .rm-opt-text { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; min-width: 0; }
    #rmForm .rm-opt-title { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--fg-default); }
    #rmForm .rm-opt-hint { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.4; }
    #rmForm .rm-opt-notes { align-items: start; }
    @@media (max-width: 900px) {
        #rmForm .rm-opt { grid-template-columns: 16px minmax(0, 1fr); row-gap: 8px; }
        #rmForm .rm-opt > .rm-opt-control { grid-column: 2; }
    }
    #rmForm .rm-sub {
        margin: 0 0 0 32px; padding: 10px 12px 12px; border-left: 2px solid var(--primary-200);
        background: var(--bg-subtle); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    #rmForm .rm-sub-row { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; gap: 16px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
    #rmForm .rm-sub-row .pm-field { width: 260px; }
    #rmForm .rm-sub-hint { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--fg-muted); }
    #rmForm .rm-currency { width: 160px; }
    #rmForm .rm-add { margin-top: 8px; }

    /* Compact grids: tighter cells, 30px controls. */
    #rmForm .rm-compact td, #rmForm .rm-compact th { padding: 6px 8px; }
    #rmForm .rm-compact .pm-input { height: 30px; padding: 4px 8px; font-size: 12px; }
    #rmForm .rm-compact td .pm-input[type="number"] { min-width: 64px; }
    #rmForm .rm-sub .pm-table-wrap { background: var(--bg-surface); }

    /* Dimension cell: the name with its fixed code beside it, the
       description below in a quieter, smaller field. */
    #rmForm td.rm-name-cell { min-width: 280px; white-space: normal; }
    #rmForm .rm-name-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
    #rmForm .rm-name-row .pm-input { flex: 1 1 auto; font-weight: 600; }
    #rmForm .rm-code {
        flex: none; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
        background: var(--bg-subtle); color: var(--fg-muted);
        font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .02em;
    }
    #rmForm .rm-name-row .rm-code-input { flex: 0 0 140px; font-weight: 400; text-transform: uppercase; }
    #rmForm .rm-compact .pm-input.rm-desc { margin-top: 4px; height: 28px; color: var(--fg-secondary); }
    #rmForm td.rm-center { text-align: center; }
    #rmForm .rm-levels td { background: var(--bg-subtle); }
    #rmForm .rm-chip, #rmRoot .rm-chip {
        display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
        background: var(--bg-subtle); color: var(--neutral-700); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600;
    }

    /* Save / Discard / Publish at the end of the form, not in a card. */
    #rmForm .rm-actions { display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; align-items: center; gap: 8px; margin: 4px 0 16px; }
    #rmForm .rm-actions .pm-form-message { margin: 0 auto 0 0; }
</style>

<partial name="Partials/_workflow-common" />
<script src="~/js/RiskCentre/risk-methodology.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
